Part 5: Detailed Data Insights & Findings
&Target Distribution: The overall employee attrition rate in the cleaned dataset stands at 39.36%, pointing to substantial turnover pressure.
&Age Demographics: Highest employee concentration is centered around young professionals (27–30 age group), who also exhibit higher mobility.
&Geographical Hubs: Bangalore represents the largest workforce Hub, followed by Pune and New Delhi.
&Education Dynamics: Employees with Bachelors degrees dominate the workforce (71 .3%), followed by Masters (23.0%) and PhDs (5.6%).
&Payment Tier Pressure: Lower payment tiers experience heavier attrition pressure compared to Tier 3.
&Tenure & Experience: Employees with lower domain experience (0–3 years) display a higher tendency to leave compared to tenured staff.
